1. Geographies that do not work properly.
1991 census tracts
Some vector tiles have information in second block:
example:
1991_ct Polygon
missing ID
CA	933
CT_NAME	238.01
CA_CTNAME	933238.01
1991_ct Polygon
missing ID
CA	933
CT_NAME	238.01
CT_CODE	3924
PROV	59
program expects the first block to have all the needed information.

2001-2006 dissemination areas
GEO_CODE does not match DAUID.
Example: GEO_CODE: 59150253648 and DAUID: 59153648
The GEO_NAME associated with GEO_CODE: 59150253648 is the same as the DAUID.
1996 enumeration areas do not have this problem.

1981 provinces, census divisions, census subdivisions show values but are grey in colour.
1986 provinces, census subdivisions show values but are grey in colour.
1991 provinces, census divisions, census subdivisions show values but are grey in colour.

2021: FED 2013 and FED 2023 both do not work. FED 2013: The value is shown but the map is grey in colour. For FED 2023: Value is N/A.